{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>Are you not</b> — Yefet said: The women of the Cushites are unrestricted [in marital relations], and no man knows who his father is, but you were sons of one father. You are not like the Philistines from Caphtor and Aram from Kir, who intermingled. And it is possible: the sense of \"Are you not like the Cushites to me, O children of Israel\" is as follows — \"Did I not bring Israel up?\" is already known, for I am your father. And so Moses said: \"Is he not your father who created you\" (Deuteronomy 32:6)." "<b>And the mem of \"from the land\"</b> — serves on account of others, and so it is: \"I brought you up from Egypt, and the Philistines from Caphtor, and Aram from Kir.\""], :book :amos, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Amos -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/amos"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:18:41.491541255Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}